From: Alexander Hansen Færøy <ahf@torproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Define SIO_UDP_NETRESET for older MinGW headers

Backport of https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/29826 (including its
follow-up style fix), for OpenSSL 3.5.5 and 3.6.1. Later patch releases
already contain this workaround.

diff --git a/ssl/quic/quic_reactor.c b/ssl/quic/quic_reactor.c
--- a/ssl/quic/quic_reactor.c
+++ b/ssl/quic/quic_reactor.c
@@ -78,4 +78,10 @@
 #if defined(OPENSSL_SYS_WINDOWS)
+
+/* Work around for MinGW builds. */
+#if defined(__MINGW32__) && !defined(SIO_UDP_NETRESET)
+#define SIO_UDP_NETRESET _WSAIOW(IOC_VENDOR, 15)
+#endif
+
 /*
  * On Windows recvfrom() may return WSAECONNRESET when destination port
  * used in preceding call to sendto() is no longer reachable. The reset
